/-!
# Rigidity of the quotient stages and the formal spectrum as an étale chart

For an object `B^∧` of the category of Stacks 0DEF, the quotient stages `B ⧸ JB` at the weak
ideals of definition `J` of `A` are rigid: a map of quotient stages at `J` lifts uniquely to every
smaller weak ideal of definition, by the étale lifting of Stacks 0ALI. Moreover the formal
spectrum `Spf B^∧ ⟶ Spf A` is an object of the category of Stacks 0DEE.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.FormalSpace.EtaleCompletion.existsUnique_stageHom_of_le`: rigidity of the
  quotient stages below a weak ideal of definition.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.FormalSpace.EtaleCompletion.exists_isAffineEtaleFormalChart_formalSpectrumMap`:
  the formal spectrum of an object of the category of Stacks 0DEF is an affine étale chart of
  `Spf A`.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0DEF](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0DEF)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0DEE](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0DEE)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0ALI](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0ALI)
-/

@[expose] public section

